# Shipyard Examples — credentials for the `keys/` and `harness/` tiers.
#
# Nothing here is needed for the `offline/`, `node/` or `docker/` tiers.
# Copy this file to .env, fill in the providers you want to exercise, and
# export the variables (or run with `env $(cat .env | xargs) ...`).
# Never commit a filled-in .env.

# --- LLM providers (examples/keys/) -------------------------------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=              # Google AI Studio key
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Ollama runs locally and needs no key; point this at your instance if it
# is not the default one.
OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434

# --- Remote agent protocol (examples/keys/) ------------------------------
# Base URL of a Remote VPC worker (see the remote-agent-protocol docs).
# The `remote` plugin POSTs <endpoint>/task.
SHIPYARD_REMOTE_AGENT_URL=

# --- CLI harnesses (examples/harness/) ------------------------------------
# The harnesses read their own provider credentials; e.g.
#   claude-code   -> ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   codex         -> OPENAI_API_KEY
#   gemini-cli    -> GEMINI_API_KEY / GOOGLE_API_KEY
#   opencode      -> its own auth (models.dev)
#   aider         -> ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY
